{{also|diploïd}}
{{wikipedia}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{confix|diplo|oid|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|cytology}} Of a cell, having a pair of each type of [[chromosome]], one of the pair being derived from the [[ovum]] and the other from the [[spermatozoon]]. Most [[somatic cell]]s of higher organisms are diploid.
# {{lb|en|cytology}} Of an organism, having diploid cells.
# {{lb|en|crystallography}} Of a certain [[symmetry]] [[class]] with 24 [[congruent]] [[irregular]] [[quadrilateral]] [[face]]s.

